    "problem_statement": "Protocol switch proposals not properly handled when processing client switch events\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen processing client switch proposals, the connection state machine incorrectly removes switch proposals from the pending set instead of adding them. This causes protocol switching to fail unexpectedly.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport h11\nfrom h11._state import ConnectionState, _SWITCH_UPGRADE\n\n# Create a connection state and propose a protocol switch\ncs = ConnectionState()\ncs.process_client_switch_proposal(_SWITCH_UPGRADE)\n\n# Check if the switch proposal was properly added\nprint(\"Switch proposal in pending set:\", _SWITCH_UPGRADE in cs.pending_switch_proposals)\n# Expected: True\n# Actual: False\n```\n\nThe issue manifests when trying to perform protocol upgrades or CONNECT requests where the client proposes a switch but the proposal is not tracked properly in the connection state."
